    <li>Select from dropdown: <code>GitHub Copilot</code>, <code>GitHub Copilot Chat</code>, or <code>GitHub Copilot Language Server</code></li>
    <li>Reproduce the issue, then copy the log output</li>
</ol>
<details><summary>Proxy / Certificate Settings</summary>
<ul>
    <li><code>http.proxy</code> — in VS Code Settings for proxy URL</li>
    <li><code>http.proxyStrictSSL</code> — set to <code>false</code> if using SSL inspection (temporary)</li>
    <li><code>NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS</code> — environment variable for custom CA certificates</li>
</ul>
<p>Ref: <a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/setup/network" target="_blank" style="color:var(--color-accent)">VS Code Network Settings</a></p>
</details>`,

    jetbrains: `<strong>JetBrains IDEs — Copilot Network Diagnostics</strong>
<ol>
    <li>Go to <code>Tools → GitHub Copilot → Log Diagnostics</code></li>
    <li>Go to <code>Tools → GitHub Copilot → Log CA Certificates</code> — shows trusted certificates</li>
    <li>Check the <code>idea.log</code>: <code>Help → Show Log in Explorer/Finder</code></li>
</ol>
<strong>Proxy Settings:</strong>
<ul>
    <li><code>Settings → Appearance & Behavior → System Settings → HTTP Proxy</code></li>
    <li>Supports manual proxy, PAC URL, and authentication</li>
</ul>
<details><summary>Certificate Trust Store</summary>
<ul>
    <li>JetBrains uses the JVM truststore by default</li>
    <li><code>Settings → Tools → Server Certificates</code> — manage accepted certificates</li>
    <li>To add a custom CA: import into the JVM cacerts or use <code>-Djavax.net.ssl.trustStore</code></li>
</ul>
</details>`,

    vs: `<strong>Visual Studio — Copilot Network Diagnostics</strong>
<ol>
    <li>Go to <code>View → Output</code></li>
    <li>Select <code>GitHub Copilot</code> from the "Show output from" dropdown</li>
    <li>Look for connection errors, authentication failures, or timeout messages</li>
</ol>
<strong>Proxy Settings:</strong>
<ul>
    <li>Visual Studio uses the system proxy settings (IE/Windows proxy)</li>
    <li>Ref: <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/visualstudio/install/install-and-use-visual-studio-behind-a-firewall-or-proxy-server" target="_blank" style="color:var(--color-accent)">Visual Studio behind a firewall</a></li>
</ul>
<details><summary>Troubleshooting</summary>
<ul>
    <li>Check <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\\GitHub\\Copilot\\Logs</code> for detailed log files</li>
    <li>Enable verbose logging: <code>Tools → Options → GitHub → Copilot → Advanced → Verbose Logging</code></li>
</ul>
</details>`,

    xcode: `<strong>Xcode — Copilot Network Diagnostics</strong>
<p>GitHub Copilot for Xcode runs as a separate background process.</p>
<ol>
    <li>Check the Copilot extension status in the menu bar icon</li>
    <li>View logs: <code>~/Library/Logs/GitHubCopilot/</code></li>
    <li>Restart the extension: quit and relaunch the Copilot for Xcode app</li>
</ol>
<strong>Proxy Settings:</strong>
<ul>
    <li>Uses macOS system proxy settings (System Settings → Network → Proxies)</li>
    <li>Set <code>HTTPS_PROXY</code> environment variable if needed</li>
</ul>`
};

function renderIdeGuide() {
    document.getElementById('ide-content').innerHTML = IDE_GUIDES[currentIdeTab];
}

function switchIdeTab(tab, el) {
    currentIdeTab = tab;
    document.querySelectorAll('.ide-tab').forEach(t => t.classList.remove('active'));
    el.classList.add('active');
    renderIdeGuide();
}

// ============================================================
// UTILITIES
// ============================================================
function flashButton(btn, msg) {
    const orig = btn.textContent;
    btn.textContent = `✓ ${msg}`;
    setTimeout(() => btn.textContent = orig, 2000);
}

function downloadFile(filename, content, type) {
    const blob = new Blob([content], { type });
    const a = document.createElement('a');
    a.href = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
    a.download = filename;
    a.click();
    URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href);
}

// Initialize IDE guide
renderIdeGuide();
</script>
</body>
</html>
